Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:47:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 085/116] LOCAL: drm/sysfb: simpledrm: Vote interconnect
 bandwidth for the framebuffer

The display engine keeps scanning out the firmware framebuffer, but no
driver votes bandwidth for it. With the SM7250 interconnect driver, the
multimedia NoC and DDR drop low enough for the scanout to underrun
(flicker, artifacts). Hold a vote on each path of the
simple-framebuffer node's interconnects property: the scanout rate as
average and an optional peak-kBps property (default twice the
scanout rate) as peak. Not for upstream; goes away with the real
display driver.

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

